\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\lang1040\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. What shall I do my God to love,
\par My loving God to praise?
\par The lingth, and breadth, and height to prove,
\par And depth of sovereign grace?
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Thy sovereign grace to all extends,
\par Immense and unconfined: 
\par From age to age it never ends;
\par It reaches all mankind.
\par \pard\tx960\tab 
\par \pard\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Throughout the world its breadth is known,
\par Wide as infinity;
\par So wide it never passed by one,
\par Or it had passed by me.
\par \pard\tx1540\tab 
\par \pard\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. My trespass was grown up to heaven;
\par But far above the skies,
\par In Christ abundantly forgiven,
\par I see Thy mercies rise.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. The depth of all-redeeming love
\par What angel tongue can tell?
\par O may I to the utmost prove
\par The gift unspeakable.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 6\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 6. Come quickly, gracious Lord, and take
\par Possession of Thine own;
\par My longing heart vouchasfe to make
\par Thine everlasting throne. 
\par                           Amen.
\par \lang1033\f1 
\par \cf1\lang1040\ul\b\f2\fs16 
\par }

